  "structure": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Through the prayers of our holy Fathers, Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us. Amen."
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Auf die Gebete unserer heiligen Väter, Herr Jesus Christus, unser Gott, erbarme Dich unser. Amen."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "r1",
      "kind": "annotation",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Then three times the Paschal Troparion in Tone 5:"
        },
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Dann dreimal das Ostertroparion im 5. Ton:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b3-msn8ttu3",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Christus ist erstanden von den Toten,",
            "hat zertreten im Tode den Tod,",
            "und denen in den Gräbern",
            "das Leben geschenkt."
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Christ is risen from the dead,",
            "trampling down death by death,",
            "and upon those in the tombs",
            "bestowing life."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b4-msn8tzri",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Χριστός ανέστη εκ νεκρών,",
            "θανάτω θάνατον πατήσας,",
            "και τοις εν τοις μνήμασι,",
            "ζωὴν χαρισάμενος!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Χριστός ανέστη εκ νεκρών,",
            "θανάτω θάνατον πατήσας,",
            "και τοις εν τοις μνήμασι,",
            "ζωὴν χαρισάμενος!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b5-msn8u4z2",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Христос воскресе из мертвых,",
            "смертию смерть поправ,",
            "и сущим во гробех живот даровав!"
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Христос воскресе из мертвых,",
            "смертию смерть поправ,",
            "и сущим во гробех живот даровав!"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b6-msn8v66f",
      "kind": "heading",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Auferstehungshymnus im 6. Ton"
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Hymn of the Resurrection in Tone 6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b7-msn8vgcw",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Die Auferstehung Christi haben wir geschaut, / so lasset uns anbeten den heiligen Herrn Jesus, / Den allein sündelosen. / Vor Deinem Kreuze fallen wir nieder, o Christus, / und Deine heilige Auferstehung besingen und verherrlichen wir. / Denn Du bist unser Gott, / außer Dir kennen wir keinen anderen. / Deinen Namen rufen wir an. / Kommt, all ihr Gläubigen, / lasset uns anbeten die heilige Auferstehung Christi. / Denn siehe, durch das Kreuz ist Freude gekommen in die ganze Welt. / Allezeit lobsingen wir dem Herrn / und preisen Seine Auferstehung. / Denn Er hat die  Kreuzigung erlitten // und durch den  Tod den Tod zertreten."
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Having beheld the Resurrection of Christ, / let us worship the holy Lord Jesus, / the only sinless One. / We fall down before Thy Cross, O Christ, / and we hymn and glorify Thy holy Resurrection. / For Thou art our God, / and we know none other besides Thee. / We call upon Thy name. / Come, all ye faithful, / let us worship the holy Resurrection of Christ. / For behold, through the Cross joy has come into all the world. / Ever blessing the Lord, we hymn / and praise His Resurrection. / For He has endured the Cross // and by death has trampled down death."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b8-msn8ws11",
      "kind": "heading",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Hypakoi im 4. Ton:"
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "text": "Hypakoe in Tone 4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b9-msn8x1js",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "Die Frauen um Maria kamen dem Tagesanbruch zuvor, / und fanden den Stein vom Grabe weggewälzt, / da hörten sie von dem Engel: / „Ihn, der in ewigem Lichte ist,/ was sucht ihr Ihn wie einen Menschen bei den Toten? / Schauet die Grabtücher und laufet und verkündet der Welt, / daß erstanden ist der Herr, der getötet den Tod. // Denn Er ist der Sohn Gottes, der da errettet das Menschengeschlecht."
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            "The women with Mary came before the dawn, / and found the stone rolled away from the tomb, / and heard from the angel: / “Why do you seek as a mortal among the dead / Him who abides in everlasting light? / Behold the grave-clothes, run and proclaim to the world / that the Lord is risen, who has put death to death. // For He is the Son of God, who saves the human race."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b10-msn8xgkt",
      "kind": "verse",
      "translations": [
        {
          "lang": "de",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "t": "note",
                "v": "Dann vierzigmal:"
              },
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": " Herr, erbarme Dich!"
              }
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "lang": "en",
          "variant": "standard",
          "lines": [
            [
              {
                "t": "note",
                "v": "Then forty times:"
              },
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": " Lord, have mercy!"
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
